6:27Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.6 rc1\nNot reproducible in 4.5.1\n\n### System information\n\nW10\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen a Resource referred by theme override is not found, the engine may crash.\nFor example:\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/895630e853b7f389c2a3de5cfe02ef433f7b8c23/scene/gui/panel.cpp#L43-L45\n\nIf `panel_style` happens to be null, there will be crash.\n\nNormally this is not possible. You can't assign a null for a theme override, and even if it's somehow null, the style should fall back to the default theme, making the style effectively guaranteed to exist.\n\nWell, before 4.6 anyway xd\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Add a Panel\n2. Create a StyleBox Resource and save it to a file\n3. Assign the StyleBox to the `panel` property in Panel's theme overrides\n4. Close the scene\n5. Remove the StyleBox file\n6. Reopen the scene (you need to Open Anyway due to missing dependency)\n7. Crash\n\nDoes not happen if the missing StyleBox is in Theme instead of override.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[stylecrashox.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24724469/stylecrashox.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https: